# Port Plan — Step 11: A Terminal UI (Ruby → Python)

Port the step-11 delta: `Boukensha.repl()` gains a `tui:` keyword (default
`True`) that wraps the plain-text REPL in a full-screen terminal UI — a
scrollable conversation viewport, a live progress line while the agent works, a
single-line input box, and an always-on status bar.

**The REPL keeps owning all session logic** — turn counting, slash commands,
agent dispatch. The TUI only replaces how it reads input and writes output.

> **This plan follows the instructor's `11_tui` Python port plan.** Its three
> judgment calls are adopted verbatim (§3). What it does *not* carry is that
> plan's assumptions about this repository's layout, which differ in five
> concrete places — §2 lists them, because following the plan literally would
> put code in the wrong files.

